Right; it says it will run faster *without* DBLIT, but that you will
get flicker.  What isn't mentioned is the amount of memory the thing
uses w/o DBLIT, I can't run it on my 24M AViiON if I leave out DBLIT.
With DBLIT it's pretty slow, but...

My real problem is this: there doesn't seem to be anything to the game
except the demo!  Am I missing something?  I let it run through the
demo but that's the only level available.  It was nice to watch on my
color AV, but that's about it, and no docs on the level file syntax
(not that I'd have time to make any anyway :-)

As for usleep, this is what I use (culled from Patrick J. Naughton's
excellent xlock package) on SYSV-like machines... saves a little setup
over select:

    #include <stdlib.h>
    #include <poll.h>

    int
    usleep(usec)
        unsigned long usec;
    {
        poll((struct poll *) 0, (size_t) 0, usec / 1000);
    }
